y she has tears in her eyes  and the footage is playing in Reverse  making it look like she's moving away  from the viewer as the tea rolls up her  cheek there's a painting behind her that  looks like Adam and Eve from the season  three badges that were posted on  Instagram besides that it looks like  Adams lair only there was no painting  like that there so this could very well  be an alternate version of the area  under the church the trailer ends with  Adam doing something with the god  particle at the power plant he flips the  switch or perhaps the device we saw at  the beginning of the trailer the black  blob looks more chaotic and unstable  than normal and it's spinning kind of  picking up speed at the end it  compresses to a bright light and then  that cuts to the closing titles it looks  like he could be destroying it but we'll  have to wait and see the closing title  tells us the final cycle begins and then  that changes to ends and then they give  us the date of the apocalypse we hear  someone say tick tock tock tick and then  just talk so it's a pretty good trailer  there's quite a lot of new stuff the  most interesting thing is this trio of  new characters we saw in the casting  announcements last year that there would  be a father and son a real-life father  and son in season 3 and I just get a  feeling from this that these are brand  new characters they walk around with the  sense of authority and it makes things  kind of confusing dark showrunner hosted  some season 3 screenshots after the  trailer dropped to go along with some of  the mirrored photos they had posted to  announce the trailer was coming after  that and watching all the behind  seen stuff he posted I was hoping we'd  have a better idea of what was going on  in the alt world but I guess that the  first trailer you can't expect too much  in those we got the best look at the  alternate characters which is shot of  Marta and Magnus you can see that his  hair's dark he's got tattoos all over  him to mark him as an alternate there's  a picture of yonis that looks like he's  looking at his house in the alternate  world there's another one of Marta  riding the bike looking like Jonah's  wearing the raincoat and then there's a  pretty interesting one of the post  apocalypse we see there's some  destruction at the plant the trees  aren't all dead and gone yet though and  this looks more like 2020 than 2053  based on the people we see there in the  cars that's all pretty exciting  considering that we knew someone arrived  to build the restricted zone and we  never saw that period of time yet  there's also this shot of Marta with the  raincoat on in the mouth of the cave  with that police tape kind of thing  going across it the popular theory now  is that this alternate world is going to  be like almost exactly the same as the  binden we've been in for the first two  seasons only Marta is going to be doing  the things that unis did in the other  world this seems a little bit too simple  to me but we'll have to see how it plays  out there definitely teasing something  that way I mean they showed these photos  of everything flipped in the background  clearly putting the yellow jacket on  marta makes you think of the onus so  it'll be interesting to see what happens  when they arrived there claudia has  mentioned visiting the world where Jonas  doesn't exist this could certainly fit  the bill so it'll be interesting to see  what happens when he does arrive Adam  seems to be going forward with his plan  more or less less he's laid it out he  looks to be trying to destroy the world  and be interesting to see if he's  working with this trio of new characters  or if they are somehow his opposite I  got a lot of things bouncing around in  my head but I think I'll leave this  video here and then put together some  Theory videos over the next month while  we wait for the season let me know what  you thought about the trailer what  you're most excited to learn about in 